# HEDA sample environment file.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values: `cp .env.example .env`
# `.env` is gitignored. Vite embeds `VITE_*` values at build time; only set
# the legacy keys for desktop release builds, never for a public web build.

# Optional. Base path for production web builds only (see vite.config.ts).
# Leave unset for Tauri desktop builds and local dev.
# BASE_PATH=/heda

# Legacy v1 migration keys. Old HEDA releases embedded these app-wide values
# in the binary, so they add no new exposure; keep them out of source anyway.
# They are still bundled into the frontend, so use them only for desktop
# release builds. Without both values, version 1 `.heda` files cannot be
# upgraded.
# VITE_LEGACY_FILE_PASSPHRASE=
# VITE_LEGACY_FILE_SALT=

# Release-only (CI secrets, never needed for local dev):
# TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY / TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD (updater signing)
# ANDROID_RELEASE_KEYSTORE / ANDROID_RELEASE_PASSWORD / ANDROID_RELEASE_KEY /
# ANDROID_RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD (Android APK signing)
